46    write(11, "The skill is now loaded and running. Steps 1\342\200\2236 of its MCP Workflow (`gh`, `claude-mem`, `serena`, `context7`) all require external tools/MCP servers that are **not installed** in this sandbox, so those are skipped. I'll execute the part that runs fully locally: apply the Review Checklist to the real `master..feature` diff and emit the documented Output Format.\n\n---\n\n## Code Review: PR #(local: `master..feature`)\n\n| Item | Value |\n|------|-------|\n| Type | Feature |\n| Risk | High |\n| Files | 1 file (+21/-2 lines) |\n\n### Summary\n> Adds user lookup, order listing, and login functions to `app.py`. The change introduces multiple Priority-1 security defects and a Priority-2 performance issue and must not be merged as-is.\n\n### Positives\n- `list_orders` correctly uses a **parameterized query** (`?` placeholder) for the inner statement \342\200\224 the right pattern, just applied in a bad loop.\n\n### Critical Issues\n1. **SQL Injection** - `app.py:8`\n   - Problem: `cur.execute(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = '%s'\" % user_id)` interpolates input directly into SQL.\n   - Impact: security \342\200\224 arbitrary SQL execution / data exfiltration.\n   - Fix: use a parameterized query: `cur.execute(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?\", (user_id,))`.\n2. **Hardcoded Credential** - `app.py:3`\n   - Problem: `DB_PASSWORD = \"hunter2\"` committed in source.\n   - Impact: security \342\200\224 secret leakage via VCS history.\n   - Fix: load from environment/secret manager (`os.environ[\"DB_PASSWORD\"]`); rotate the exposed value.\n3. **Sensitive Data Logged** - `app.py:20`\n   - Problem: `logging.info(... password=%s ...)` writes the plaintext password to logs.\n   - Impact: security \342\200\224 credential disclosure in log sinks.\n   - Fix: never log passwords; log only `user` and outcome.\n\n### Major Issues\n1. **N+1 Query** - `app.py:14-18` - Fix: replace the per-id loop with a single `WHERE uid IN (...)` (or `executemany`/join) query.\n2. **Insecure auth comparison** - `app.py:21` - Fix: compare against a salted hash with `hmac.compar"..., 7297) = 7297
